<h3>Remote Slicing</h3>
<p>Models are sliced on your PC by CuraEngine, with the Cura settings you last used. Two things run on the PC:</p>
<ol>
    <li><strong>The Cura plugin "Remote Slicing Snapshot".</strong> Drag <code>RemoteSlicingSnapshot-&lt;version&gt;.curapackage</code>
        onto Cura's window and restart Cura. It saves your active printer, profile and materials every time they
        change, so jobs use the settings Cura was last closed with. Cura does not need to be open while slicing.</li>
    <li><strong>The PC agent.</strong> From the <code>agent</code> folder, run
        <code>python -m remote_slicing_agent setup --url http://&lt;this OctoPrint&gt;</code> and approve the
        "Remote Slicing Agent" request that pops up here in OctoPrint. Then start it with
        <code>pythonw -m remote_slicing_agent run</code>, or make it start with Windows:
        <code>python -m remote_slicing_agent install-startup</code>.</li>
</ol>
<p class="muted">SolidWorks parts are converted through the Cura SolidWorks plugin on the PC. "From PC Dropbox" lists the folder
    that the Dropbox app syncs on that PC.</p>
